#X text 20 20 FLOURISH PROBE -- two ways to make one 404 pad stutter slower and slower while its pitch falls \, both retriggering on the 404. The rules are flourish.lua beside this file. Not part of Cut It: a menu patch in /sdcard/Patches/! debug/ \, and loading it stops the instrument until Cut It is selected again., f 120;
#X text 20 1000 KEYS (white \, from the lowest C): C retrigger on chromatic ch 16 falling 48 to 36. D retrigger the selected pad at its own pitch. E pad once then DJFX Looper on 10 ms later with SPEED falling. F the same with the loop on 230 ms later. G the selected pad once. A stop: LOOP SW off and SPEED back to normal., f 120;
#X text 20 1080 KNOBS: 1 run length 1 to 6 s. 2 first gap 10 to 150 ms. 3 last gap 80 to 800 ms. 4 the looper's final SPEED 5 to 100 percent. Strike a pad on the 404 to select it. The looper's CCs go on the 404's channel 1 (BUS 1): CC 17 SPEED and CC 18 LOOP SW \, per the v3.00 MIDI chart., f 120;
#X text 300 380 midiOutGate 0 and midiInGate 0 after mother's own push half a second in: mother echoes the keys to every port \, and the 404's pads would come back as keys (ref/module/boot.md)., f 34;
#X text 1100 420 notein fires right to left \, so the channel and velocity are in before the note arrives hot., f 40;
